From 0b616255cbb5816528a50797d516f52a6b74e4b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alistair Reay <5599065+alistairreay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Feb 2026 15:43:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add VNC Authentication (type 2) and RFB 3.3 support
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Implement legacy VNC Authentication (security type 2) using DES
challenge-response for compatibility with clients like macOS Screen
Sharing that don't support VeNCrypt/RSA-AES.

Key changes:
- Add VNC Auth with DES challenge-response (nettle) in auth/vnc-auth.c
- Support RFB 3.3/3.7/3.8 version negotiation in on_version_message()
- RFB 3.3: server sends single uint32 security type (not count+list)
- RFB 3.3: SecurityResult has no reason string on failure
- Fix CPIXEL calculation to follow RFB spec (use pixel format conditions
  instead of depth field) — fixes ZRLE corruption with depth=32 clients
- Expose nvnc_set_vnc_auth_password() public API
